guamp: metal2vulkan bridge patch 0050, a commit's submission on the scheduler's thread, off Core Animation's render thread

fin53 (live-20261106-092610, 271 -> 331 s, the "searching" status-bar animation at 53 fps): backboardd's render thread spent
16.1 ms CPU of every 18.6 ms frame (U row), 11.5 ms of them inside the bridge (A0/A1 rows): draws 3.9 ms (22 draws, 178 us
each: settle 39, cmd 19, heap 26, rec 95), pass opens 0.9 ms, closes 3.5 ms (9 encoders, 268 us each), blits 1.3 ms, commit
1.6 ms of which the submission (B row `sub`) 1.39 ms: the scheduler's pass made inline on the committing thread (planning,
vkQueueSubmit, Turnip's Darwin submit with the kernel's cache maintenance of imports, a wait for a free ring slot).
Bridge patch 0050 (crates/metal2vulkan-runtime scheduler/mod.rs and inbox.rs): Scheduler::commit leaves the commit in the inbox
(Inbox::post) and wakes the scheduler's own thread (user-interactive), which takes it in, in commit order, as it already does for
a commit left to a pass under way; submission handlers run there (as for a commit handed off). NMB_SUBMIT_INLINE=1 (boot line
through guamp-m2v-env, 0019) keeps the pass inline as before. The B row's `sub` then measures only the hand-off.
Host (lavapipe, examples/draw_costs, 3 interleaved pairs of 580 frames): commit 91-122 us -> 35-38 us on the encoding thread.
Applies after every earlier bridge patch (scheduler/ is touched by none of them).

